samsung's new galaxy s22 ultra is  currently breaking the tech internet not  only on the android side but also for  apple fans because this is the first  time in a while that i think samsung  knocked it out of the park with the  design and feature set and it's giving  apple's iphone 13 pro max some serious  competition so before i get into  comparing all the specs and new features  to see if the new s22 ultra can actually  take the smartphone crown away from  apple i want to get into samsung's  clever master plan for how they're  marketing this new ultra smartphone but  first i want to mention that my wife and  i just had our second son eli and i'm  finally back to work and ready to bring  you guys some more tech related content  so let's jump right into it if you  didn't already know samsung discontinued  the galaxy note flagship phone series  last year when for the first time in  many years they didn't release an  updated model and that really sucked  because we absolutely loved the previous  galaxy note 20 ultra which came with a  beautiful squarish design a built-in s  pen and an amazing camera bump layout  but last year samsung decided to release  their two new foldable phones instead  the z-fold three and the z flip three so  they've basically made it apparent that  their foldable phones have now replaced  the note series as their flagship  because in reality they already have two  high-end smartphone lineups a year the s  series and the foldables so doing all  three including the notes would be too  much so they made just about the best  choice they could have made in my  opinion they simply took the note design  and rebranded it as the s22 ultra with a  design that's almost identical to the  note 20 ultra now this is very clever  because it sets the ultra model apart  from the lower end s22 models which have  a completely different design and let me  add that i absolutely can't stand the  chunky notch that kind of melts into the  frame it just looks horribly ugly so  thankfully they got rid of it for the  ultra model and gave each camera lens  its own separate bump which i think  looks incredibly clean and it's part of  the reason why i think this phone will  be so successful not to mention this  great looking white model and to be  honest the combination of the beautiful  camera layout the matte glass finish the  rounded display edges and the super  clean and high quality display with just  a single camera cut out definitely gives  the iphone 13 pro max a run for its  money because i mean it still has that  ugly notch that i'm honestly getting  sick of and of course it still has the  old usb 2.0  lightning port so the hardware side is  kind of dragging along compared to the  new galaxy s22 ultra now in my opinion i  still really like the camera bump on the  13 pro max better because of the whole  three-step design that looks very clean  and professional but the new one on the  ultra looks very good as well now the  next thing i want to talk about is the  cameras and samsung's honestly doing a  very good job in this department while  apple has caught up pretty well with the  new 13 pro max i've gotta hand it to  samsung because they've been improving  their 108 megapixel main camera over the  past couple of years and now they're  optimizing it for nighttime photos and  videos and i'm really excited to see  some comparisons because it was already  so close with last year's s21 ultra but  the major advantage comes down to the  additional 10x space zoom lens which  pumps out incredibly sharp long range  zoom photos which is something that's  simply not possible on the iphone right  now and we're not rumored to get that  until the iphone 15 pro models but i do  want to mention that we've already  ordered an s22 ultra and we're gonna be  doing our popular unbiased blind camera  comparison so if you're not already  subscribed do so right now so you don't  miss out now moving forward i want to  get into display quality and this right  here is very impressive the new s22  ultra can go down to one hertz refresh  rate compared to 10 on the iphone 13 pro  max which allows it to save battery life  while using things like always on  display mode but that's actually one of  the things that's rumored for the iphone  14 pro model so hopefully we get that  later this year but in terms of display  quality samsung has one upped apple once  again not only does the s22 ultra have a  higher 1440p resolution compared to  1284p for the 13 pro max but you can now  finally use 120hz at the same time and  that's probably because it comes with a  5 000 milliamp hour battery compared to  4352 on the 13 pro max so it'll be  interesting to see the battery life  difference when mr who's the boss gets  that done but getting back to the  display samsung is now advertising a  massive  1750 peak brightness compared to apple's  1200 nits which is actually a huge  difference and should give you better  looking hdr content now moving over to  authentication the s22 ultra simply has  a single hole punch for the high quality  40 megapixel selfie camera because they  don't use a sophisticated face id like  system instead they have the under  display ultrasonic fingerprint scanner  and to be honest this has been improving  over the years and it's now very good at  what it does however it's still not  perfect because it obviously doesn't  work for anyone who wears gloves and it  has issues when your fingers are wet or  if it's really cold outside in the  winter and now i know face id on the  iphone has caused issues for a lot of  people who wear masks but apple has  finally updated it and fixed every  single issue now allowing face id to  work perfectly fine with a mask on and  even with glasses added on top of that  so it's honestly by far the best  solution out there right now being so  much better than the fingerprint scanner  on the samsung flagship phones but on a  positive note the s pen now comes  included and it fits into the body just  like it did on the previous note so  that's a really nice added bonus but now  getting into some of the other specs i  really like how it comes with wi-fi 6e  and bluetooth 5.2 compared to only wi-fi  6 and bluetooth 5 on the iphone which  honestly was a huge disappointment when  apple revealed it and on top of that the  iphone still has just 6 gigs of ram  compared to 8 on the base model s22  ultra going all the way up to a massive  16 gigabytes which i honestly think is a  bit overkill but it guarantees that apps  simply won't close on you but in terms  of the performance department i'm  honestly a bit disappointed with the new  snapdragon 8 gen 1 ship because it's  barely improved over the old 888 chip in  terms of cpu performance and it's miles  behind the a15 bionic in the iphone and  the same thing goes for the graphics  performance as well which actually got a  nice boost but it's still way behind  apple's five core a15 especially in  terms of power usage which is definitely  a disappointment but one of the major  advantages of samsung's phones is that  they use much better cooling systems  compared to what apple uses so they're  able to handle longer gaming sessions  without the display dimming which isn't  as big of a problem on the new 13 pro  max as it was on the 12 lineup but it's  still there a little bit but with all  that said if we just break everything  down and look at the s22 ultra for what  it is it's probably hands down the best  android phone ever made because it  combines some of the best tech hardware  out there into one device that honestly  looks really nice and clean but unlike  the days of the past this new flagship  is actually a hundred dollars more  expensive than apple's 13 pro max so  it's going to be a tough decision for  people that are in the middle and there  are actually some really awesome iphone  features that you just can't get on a  samsung flagship like magsafe which is  one of my favorite iphone features of  all time since it makes mounting it in  my car so much easier and i also love  the new mac safe wallet and on top of  that apple software has been getting so  good recently that it's really hard to  give up especially with new features  coming soon like tap to pay and even the  digital license feature as well so all  in all i think it's going to be a close  one between these two and it's really  going to come down to both the display  and camera performance which we're going  to be comparing very soon when we get  our hands on this new phone so if you  haven't already subscribed go ahead and  click the circle above to do so right  now and definitely check out one of  those two videos right over there thanks  for watching and we'll see you in the  next video  [Music]
 

